@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+REM scalar IEEE runtime source port
+
+Upstream: LLVM compiler-rt 15.0.7
+Archive SHA256:
+353832c66cce60931ea0413b3c071faad59eefa70d02c97daa8978b15e4b25b7
+License: LICENSE.TXT (Apache 2.0 with LLVM exception)
+
+Build with the repaired native REM compiler:
+    CC=/absolute/path/to/chibicc-integer bash build-native.sh
+
+This builds only scalar binary32/binary64 arithmetic, comparisons, conversions,
+and the software rounding-mode support. No CMake, Python, complex arithmetic,
+128-bit integer support, kernel modification, or QEMU modification is needed.
+REM uses the little-endian ILP32 ABI, with wide values passed low word first.
+
+Port changes:
+- Recognize REM's little-endian layout.
+- Respect the compiler's lack of complex support.
+- Replace unavailable bit-count and prediction builtins with ordinary C.
+- Exclude unused complex-math helpers requiring unsupported math builtins.
+- Select software-only conversion code with __SOFTFP__.
+- Construct zero return values through integer union members so an initial
+  integer-only compiler can build the floating runtime without parsing decimal
+  floating literals or recursively calling a not-yet-repaired float helper.
+
+The default software environment rounds to nearest-even and has no hardware
+floating exception environment. This is not a hardware fenv implementation.
+
+Link native/ieee-runtime.o explicitly BEFORE libc/libgcc. An archive alone is
+not sufficient: legacy libc references can otherwise pull the old non-IEEE
+floating helpers from libgcc. The source-kit compiler driver accepts the
+absolute object path through CHIBICC_REM_SOFTFLOAT.
+
+All 29 selected sources built natively on REM. The repaired runtime and
+relinked native compiler pass ieee-soft-float.c, covering literals, arithmetic,
+conversions, NaN, signed zero and subnormals (request 048). This is not full
+compiler/libc or userland qualification.
+The existing REM_CHIBICC_BUGLOG.md records the native encoding failure as
+NU-22; ieee-soft-float.c supplies representative numerical acceptance.
--- a/build-native.sh	1970-01-01 01:00:00.000000000 +0100
+++ b/build-native.sh	2026-10-06 23:17:00.686168567 +0100
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+#!/bin/bash
+set -eu
+case $0 in */*) cd "${0%/*}" ;; esac
+CC=${CC:-chibicc}
+mkdir -p native
+objects=
+for file in addsf3 adddf3 subsf3 subdf3 mulsf3 muldf3 divsf3 divdf3 \
+    comparesf2 comparedf2 extendsfdf2 truncdfsf2 \
+    fixsfsi fixdfsi fixunssfsi fixunsdfsi fixsfdi fixdfdi fixunssfdi fixunsdfdi \
+    floatsisf floatsidf floatdisf floatdidf floatunsisf floatunsidf \
+    floatundisf floatundidf fp_mode; do
+    echo "CC IEEE runtime $file.c"
+    "$CC" -D__SOFTFP__=1 -c "lib/builtins/$file.c" -o "native/$file.o"
+    objects="$objects native/$file.o"
+done
+ld -r -T ../rem-reloc.ld -o native/ieee-runtime.o $objects
+echo "IEEE runtime built; link native/ieee-runtime.o before libc and libgcc."
